render: convert the LF frame of a VarDCT frame to three float color channels before reading the
LF coefficients from it. A Modular LF frame of an image that is not XYB encoded keeps integer
samples, and one of a grayscale image has a single color channel; render_vardct used the buffer as
three XYB float channels as is and panicked (vardct/mod.rs: range end index 3 out of range for
slice of length 1; image.rs: called `Option::unwrap()` on a `None` value in as_color_floats).
libjxl converts every Modular frame, LF frames included, to float and replicates a gray channel
(ModularImageToDecodedRect); this uses the conversion of jxl-oxide's own Modular output path
(clone_gray, convert_modular_color). Test: lf_frame_color_channels
(crates/jxl-oxide-tests/tests/lf_frame_color_channels.rs).

Upstream: not reported; the code is unchanged at upstream HEAD (c0cc4c7, 2026-08-15).

